"text":"போர்அடு","lemma":"போர்அடு","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"தானை","parts":[{"text":"தானை","lemma":"தானை","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"எவ்வி","parts":[{"text":"எவ்வி","lemma":"எவ்வி","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"மார்பின்","parts":[{"text":"மார்பின்","lemma":"மார்பின்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true},{"words":[{"surface":"எ·குஉறு","parts":[{"text":"எ·குஉறு","lemma":"எ·குஉறு","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"விழுப்புண்","parts":[{"text":"விழுப்புண்","lemma":"விழுப்புண்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பல","parts":[{"text":"பல","lemma":"பல","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"என","parts":[{"text":"என","lemma":"என","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true},{"words":[{"surface":"வைகறு","parts":[{"text":"வைகு","lemma":"வைகு","gloss":"dawn"},{"text":"அறு","lemma":"அறு","gloss":"break"}],"gloss":"dawn-breaking"},{"surface":"விடியல்","parts":[{"text":"விடியல்","lemma":"விடியல்","gloss":"early morning"}],"gloss":"early morning"},{"surface":"இயம்பிய","parts":[{"text":"இயம்பிய","lemma":"இயம்பு","gloss":"sounded"}],"gloss":"that sounded"},{"surface":"குரலே","parts":[{"text":"குரல்","lemma":"குரல்","gloss":"voice"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"the voice indeed"}]}],"literal":"May it be false! May it be false! / Without withholding flat-footed elephants to gift-seekers, / with Akutai of glorious, strong feet, appeared / like the gold-crafted discus, may it be false! / The leader of the large family of bards, wearing great ornaments, / on the chest of Evvi of the battle-slaying army, / saying 'there are many noble wounds received from spears', / the voice that sounded in the dawn-breaking early morning!","translation":"May it be false! May it be false! Like the gold-crafted discus that appeared with Akutai of glorious, strong feet—who never withheld flat-footed elephants from those seeking gifts—may it be false! The voice that sounded in the breaking dawn, saying, 'There are many noble wounds from spears on the chest of Evvi, the leader of the large family of bards, who wears great ornaments and commands a battle-slaying army!'","modern":"பொய்யாகக் கடவது! பொய்யாகக் கடவது! பரிசிலர்களுக்குப் பரந்த அடிகளையுடைய யானைகளை இல்லை என்று கூறாமல் வாரி வழங்கும், புகழும் வலிமையும் மிக்க முயற்சியும் உடைய அகுதையிடம் தோன்றிய பொன்னால் செய்யப்பட்ட திகிரி போல, விடியற்காலையில் ஒலித்த அந்தச் செய்தி பொய்யாகக் கடவது! பெரும் ஆபரணங்களை அணிந்தவனும், பாணர்களின் பெரிய சுற்றத்திற்குத் தலைவனும், போரை வெல்லும் படையை உடையவனுமாகிய எவ்வியின் மார்பில் வேல்களால் உண்டான விழுப்புண்கள் பல உள்ளன என்று விடியற்காலையில் ஒலித்த அந்தச் செய்தி பொய்யாகக் கடவது!","explanation":"The poet Veḷḷerukkilaiyār laments the death of the chieftain Vēḷ Evvi. Hearing the news at dawn that Evvi has sustained fatal wounds in battle, the poet desperately wishes that this news is false. He compares his hope for the news to be false to the legendary golden discus of Akutai, which was known for its unfailing truth or protective power. Evvi is praised as a generous patron of bards and a brave warrior who received many wounds on his chest. The poem belongs to the Potuviyal tiṇai and Kaiyaṟunilai tuṟai, expressing deep grief and helplessness over the loss of a great patron.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}